Ladybird exposes a color input’s swatch as the standard ::color-swatch,
aliased as ::-webkit-color-swatch and ::-moz-color-swatch, inside a
wrapper exposed as ::-webkit-color-swatch-wrapper, and styles both from
its default stylesheet. Blink’s ColorInputType::CreateShadowSubtree()
and WebKit’s ColorInputType::createShadowSubtree() build that same
wrapper and swatch, with those two -webkit- names, and style them from
html.css (padding 4px 2px on the wrapper, a 1px #777777 border on the
swatch). Gecko exposes just the swatch, as ::-moz-color-swatch, which
its forms.css styles the same way.
